{
 "id": "def-pur-supported-cup-functoriality-models",
 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Native Hom models and normalized operations for supported cup functoriality",
 "statement": "For the finite datum of [def-pur-conventions], define the native closed-support Hom model, the actual signed Tate targets, normalized exact inverse-image maps, Kummer extension realization, and open/closed localization sequence on each small site. These are the operations of [def-pur-supported-cup] and [def-pur-frame-class], with the boundary of [thm-pur-with-support-exactness]. The site comparison is the canonical exact inverse image. Its source and open comparison isomorphisms are uniquely normalized by restriction and inclusion. The algebra, localization and comparison predicates record precisely the corresponding equations without assuming them. The underlying Hom groups, pullbacks, cup products, normalizations and site comparisons are those of [def-pur-supported-class-operations], [def-pur-supported-class-normalizations], [def-pur-exact-derived-hom-map], [def-pur-supported-hom-site-comparison] and [def-pur-ordinary-hom-site-comparison].",
